#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c6edbe-0d21-5292-af54-3aee476000ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} {:answer/id #uuid "93a81b6f-340c-5a38-93ca-46a5ff16f29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342311} {:answer/id #uuid "2383bcff-b9da-593f-88c2-e89a2f61299a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342312} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca59082-0a28-52be-80e6-2e8a54550b5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342313} {:answer/id #uuid "8a29d6a2-873c-5695-b181-655cccae2a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c6edbe-0d21-5292-af54-3aee476000ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} :answer-field/id #uuid "40a81efe-bb81-5712-8a60-556d0e16bd14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ba1202f-23bb-59b7-8a58-51ad745d9aba" :question/math-academy-id "q-15225" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/6c70d5f15424c4d7d67a3998a785a214e46e8dfa47b83839fd99a574b2f756cf.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-1,6]$, is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(4,0)$ with radius $1.$ Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-0}\\cdot (3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a81a285c-f15c-58f0-9c84-62f3e9f26266" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099317} {:answer/id #uuid "ffca6662-3858-5473-b35f-eebdec446ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099318} {:answer/id #uuid "27ac6fb3-c4a4-5f16-af6d-dfdb68e12572" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099319} {:answer/id #uuid "512b4e23-87c8-55f8-a64a-6f0439054c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099320} {:answer/id #uuid "5f1bc557-c03e-5a50-88da-8e2e5735d95d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27ac6fb3-c4a4-5f16-af6d-dfdb68e12572" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099319} :answer-field/id #uuid "d30b6a38-e191-570c-869d-8fd60553a18c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32d27667-c963-519c-a8ec-24392218b2f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-30752" :question/problem "What is the average value of $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ on the interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }{(\\frac{1}{2})(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }(-1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15dbdf95-25d3-5705-9dda-b95d39ec2dda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342317} {:answer/id #uuid "9be1941e-5532-5a7a-8393-bb22b0656389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15dbdf95-25d3-5705-9dda-b95d39ec2dda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342317} :answer-field/id #uuid "08cc087a-9463-5e77-bef9-e6e9d28c2613" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0b37cec7-6e6c-5351-8484-5f1e038f1fd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-316302" :question/problem "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{8}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{9}}{9})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9\\pi }[(-1)^{9}-{1}^{9}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6441432-c33b-55f9-8ad3-ece97b055c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6441432-c33b-55f9-8ad3-ece97b055c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342321} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cdfcd64-e975-5f9a-a87e-656249c63b24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f43cc69-bbf5-5e06-8e03-26d2b66ad73a" :question/math-academy-id "q-344702" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/8ddd8493662174e0ddaf9bdd63b0ec382f6bb25c9079f1a339b71400b8cf3860.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-6,6],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $15$, $60$ and $9,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-6,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-15+60-9=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-6)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dad32c61-bf56-5ab6-ab8a-11cd7af4f4c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342324} {:answer/id #uuid "2d95845d-452b-5660-b2df-86636bf6cb80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342325} {:answer/id #uuid "ba37b375-a7f8-523a-bf42-0a38de161dae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342326} {:answer/id #uuid "2445c84b-78d1-54b5-9846-b12f2008db7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342327} {:answer/id #uuid "6361f8ea-bedb-5143-aeeb-290263a4480f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba37b375-a7f8-523a-bf42-0a38de161dae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342326} :answer-field/id #uuid "80f50ef6-6c7d-538f-b789-d3ce72a775a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3eb6e7c8-042a-55b7-8ed7-70afc58e2b4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74070" :question/problem "Find $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=3-2x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $1.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(3-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(3x-{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(3c-{c}^{2})-(0)] \\\\ 1 & =3-c \\\\ -2 & =-c \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
